  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1 ast-no-date-box\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n\n<p><!-- .entry-header --></p>\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Information :</strong>  </span>has released the Answer Key for the recruitment of Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Posts. This recruitment was released for 2317 posts. Applications for the MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Recruitment 2026 were accepted from 06 April 2026, to 03 May 2026. The written examination was Conducted from 15 May 2026. Candidates who had applied this form can download their MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Answer Key 2026 from the link given below.</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Madhya Pradesh Professional Selection Board (MPESB)</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Answer Key 2026</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Application Start Date : <strong>06 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Last Date : <strong>20 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Fee Payment Last Date : <strong>20 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Correction Last Date :&nbsp;<strong>25 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"background-color: #ffffff; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Form Re-Open : <strong>29 April – 03 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Exam Date : <strong>15 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Admit Card : <strong>08 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Answer Key : <strong>18 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">General, Other State :<strong> Rs. 500/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">SC, ST, OBC :<strong> Rs. 250/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">EWS, PH (Divyang) :<strong> Rs. 250/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Portal Charges : <strong>Rs. 60/- Extra&nbsp;</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates have to pay their Examination Fee Through Debit Card / Credit Card / Net Banking / UPI and Other Fee Payment Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">[adinserter block=”3″]</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Notification 2026 : Age Limit</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Age Limit As On 01 January 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Minimum Age :&nbsp;<strong>18 Years</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>40 Years (General / EWS)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>45 Years (OBC/ SC/ ST/ PH/ Female)&nbsp;</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Age Relaxation as per MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Recruitment Rules.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\"> </span>Tool – </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor 2026 : Vacancy Details</strong></span></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Total Posts : 2317 Posts</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>No. of Posts</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Nursing Officer</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">2099</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Sister&nbsp;Tutor</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">218</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Recruitment 2026 : Educational Qualification</b></span></h3>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.2633%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 70.7367%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Eligibility&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.2633%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Nursing Officer</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 70.7367%;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-section-id=\"xa5kxq\" data-start=\"97\" data-end=\"269\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">The candidate must have passed <strong data-start=\"131\" data-end=\"158\">10+2 (Higher Secondary)</strong> examination from a <strong data-start=\"178\" data-end=\"198\">recognized board</strong> with <strong data-start=\"204\" data-end=\"245\">Physics, Chemistry, and Biology (PCB)</strong> as compulsory subjects.</span></li>\n<li data-section-id=\"grhlzf\" data-start=\"271\" data-end=\"724\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">The candidate must have completed <strong data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"335\">B.Sc. Nursing (4 years)</strong> or <strong data-start=\"339\" data-end=\"399\">Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing (2 years after General Nursing)</strong> from a <strong data-start=\"407\" data-end=\"524\">nursing training institute recognized by the Madhya Pradesh Nursing Registration Council / Indian Nursing Council</strong>, with <strong data-start=\"531\" data-end=\"552\">minimum 45% marks</strong> in aggregate.</span><br data-start=\"566\" data-end=\"569\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates belonging to <strong data-start=\"596\" data-end=\"637\">reserved categories (SC, ST, and OBC)</strong> will be granted <strong data-start=\"654\" data-end=\"699\">5% relaxation in minimum qualifying marks</strong> as per government rules.</span></li>\n<li data-section-id=\"gbqs5k\" data-start=\"726\" data-end=\"844\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">The candidate must possess a <strong data-start=\"758\" data-end=\"843\">valid and active registration with the Madhya Pradesh Nurses Registration Council</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.2633%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Sister&nbsp;Tutor</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 70.7367%;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-section-id=\"10pxpz2\" data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"282\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">The candidate must have <strong data-start=\"137\" data-end=\"183\">passed 10+2 (Higher Secondary Examination)</strong> from a <strong data-start=\"191\" data-end=\"211\">recognized board</strong> with <strong data-start=\"217\" data-end=\"258\">Physics, Chemistry, and Biology (PCB)</strong> as compulsory subjects.</span></li>\n<li data-section-id=\"q2s1ah\" data-start=\"284\" data-end=\"422\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">The candidate must have <strong data-start=\"311\" data-end=\"335\">passed B.Sc. Nursing</strong> or <strong data-start=\"339\" data-end=\"387\">Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing (P.B.B.Sc. Nursing)</strong> from a <strong data-start=\"395\" data-end=\"421\">recognized institution</strong>.</span></li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1c9mk6m\" data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"557\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong data-start=\"427\" data-end=\"442\">Experience:</strong> Candidates holding <strong data-start=\"462\" data-end=\"499\">B.Sc. Nursing / P.B.B.Sc. Nursing</strong> must have <strong data-start=\"510\" data-end=\"556\">minimum 1 year of relevant work experience</strong>.</span></li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1yl1d8u\" data-start=\"559\" data-end=\"675\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">The candidate must possess <strong data-start=\"589\" data-end=\"674\">valid and active registration with the Madhya Pradesh Nurses Registration Council</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>How To Download MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Answer Key 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Open on the region wise&nbsp;<strong>Download Answer Key</strong>&nbsp;link from the&nbsp;<strong>Important Links&nbsp;</strong>box placed below.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates will be redirected to a new page.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">In this page, candidates have to fill up the required fields given as following:</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Registration ID/ Roll Number/ Name</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Date of Birth</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Father’s Name (In case of searching by name)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Captcha code</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">And Click on&nbsp;<strong>Search</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">After submitting the correct details, applicants will be able to download the Answer Key.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>MPESB Nursing Officer, Sister Tutor Recruitment 2025 : Mode of Selection</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Online Exam</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Medical Examination</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Document Verification</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">[adinserter block=”3″]</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable2\">\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"4\" data-align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #cc00